# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# riscv64 runtime env overlay for the CubeSandbox one-click installer.
#
# Copy the values you need into your deployment .env (the file install.sh reads,
# normally /usr/local/services/cubetoolbox/.one-click.env), or source this file
# before running install.sh. Every setting here exists because a component that
# the x86_64/arm64 one-click path pulls as a prebuilt Docker image has NO riscv64
# image published upstream. See deploy/one-click/RISCV64.md for the full rationale.
#
# Two data-plane strategies are provided. Pick ONE:
#   Strategy B (RECOMMENDED for riscv64): native MySQL/Redis from Yocto debs +
#           CUBE_EXTERNAL_* so install.sh skips the bundled docker-compose DB.
#   Strategy A (compose parity): build riscv64 MySQL/Redis images and point
#           CUBE_SANDBOX_MYSQL_IMAGE / _REDIS_IMAGE at them.
# Strategy B is recommended because the Yocto MySQL 8.4.11 deb links against
# OpenSSL 3.4 (libcrypto3/libssl3 >= 3.4.0), which ubuntu:24.04 (OpenSSL 3.0)
# does NOT provide — so a naive `FROM ubuntu:24.04 + dpkg -i` image has unmet
# deps. Native install on a Yocto rootfs uses the exact matching libs.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Architecture marker (consumed by the build/bundle pipeline; harmless at runtime)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ONE_CLICK_ARCH=riscv64

# PVM is x86_64-only. riscv64 uses native KVM (RISC-V H-extension), exactly like
# aarch64. Leave this at 0; install.sh's kvm_pvm probe is a natural no-op here.
CUBE_PVM_ENABLE=0

# s3lvol (SPDK/DPDK) release binaries are x86_64-only (Haswell/AVX2 baseline).
# Keep disabled on riscv64; lib/common.sh dies if you try to enable it.
ONE_CLICK_ENABLE_S3LVOL=0

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Object store: MinIO has NO riscv64 image (and Yocto has no minio recipe).
# Disable it and use the local filesystem artifact backend instead. This is a
# supported, first-class configuration (single-node/all-in-one).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CUBE_SANDBOX_MINIO_ENABLED=0
CUBE_ARTIFACT_STORE_BACKEND=fs
CUBE_OPS_STORE_BACKEND=fs

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CoreDNS: the official coredns/coredns:1.14.2 image DOES publish riscv64
# (verified via docker manifest inspect). Use Docker Hub official directly rather
# than the Tencent mirror, whose riscv64 availability is not guaranteed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CUBE_PROXY_COREDNS_IMAGE=coredns/coredns:1.14.2

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STRATEGY B (RECOMMENDED): native MySQL + Redis on the riscv64 host.
#
# 1. Install MySQL 8.4 + Redis from the Yocto riscv64 debs:
#      bash deploy/one-click/scripts/riscv64/install-native-db.sh
#    (copies/installs the debs, initializes mysqld with mysql_native_password,
#     creates the cube user, starts both services on 127.0.0.1)
# 2. Point the installer at them. With CUBE_EXTERNAL_MYSQL_HOST / _REDIS_HOST set,
#    install.sh skips the bundled docker-compose mysql/redis/minio services.
#
# The CubeSandbox MySQL DSN (pkgs/cubedb/dao/driver/mysql/mysql.go) uses plain
# TCP with no TLS and no allowPublicKeyRetrieval, so the cube user MUST use
# mysql_native_password (caching_sha2_password would fail over plaintext). The
# native-install script creates the user with that plugin.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CUBE_EXTERNAL_MYSQL_HOST=127.0.0.1
CUBE_EXTERNAL_MYSQL_PORT=3306
CUBE_EXTERNAL_MYSQL_USER=cube
CUBE_EXTERNAL_MYSQL_PASSWORD=cube_pass
CUBE_EXTERNAL_MYSQL_DB=cube_mvp

CUBE_EXTERNAL_REDIS_HOST=127.0.0.1
CUBE_EXTERNAL_REDIS_PORT=6379
CUBE_EXTERNAL_REDIS_PASSWORD=ceuhvu123

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STRATEGY A (ALTERNATIVE): bundled docker-compose DB with riscv64 images.
# Comment out the CUBE_EXTERNAL_* block above, then set these. Build the images
# with deploy/one-click/scripts/riscv64/build-db-images-riscv64.sh (requires a
# riscv64 Docker host — e.g. the L1 testbed — or buildx + qemu-user emulation).
#
# Redis: official redis:7-alpine DOES publish riscv64 (verified). Use it directly.
# CUBE_SANDBOX_REDIS_IMAGE=redis:7-alpine
#
# MySQL: no official riscv64 image. Build one from the Yocto MySQL 8.4 deb on a
# base that provides OpenSSL 3.4 (see images/mysql-riscv64/Dockerfile). MySQL 8.4
# removed --default-authentication-plugin, so override the server command to
# enable mysql_native_password at the server level instead:
# CUBE_SANDBOX_MYSQL_IMAGE=<your-registry>/cube-sandbox-mysql:8.4-riscv64
# CUBE_SANDBOX_MYSQL_COMMAND=["--mysql-native-password=ON", "--skip-name-resolve"]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# cube-* application images (P4). These have no upstream riscv64 tags; build them
# from the riscv64 binaries in _output/bin/*-riscv64 and point these vars at the
# results. Placeholders — fill in after building (see deploy/one-click/RISCV64.md).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CUBE_SANDBOX_CUBE_PROXY_IMAGE=<your-registry>/cube-proxy:riscv64
# CUBE_SANDBOX_CUBE_LCM_IMAGE=<your-registry>/cube-lifecycle-manager:riscv64
# CUBE_SANDBOX_CUBE_EGRESS_IMAGE=<your-registry>/cube-egress:riscv64
# WEB_UI_IMAGE=<your-registry>/cube-webui:riscv64
